<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI33-M5-NO-REAL-DAEMON-CI-TEST>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI33-M5-NO-REAL-DAEMON-CI-TEST" ;
  triage:title "No deterministic real-daemon admission burst test wired into Rust/CI" ;
  triage:description "arch-ctm's M5 root-cause investigation reports there is no deterministic real-daemon admission-burst test wired into Rust or CI — the existing unit tests for scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py only exercise mocked runner helpers, never a real daemon under load. This means the genuine capacity/backpressure defect surfaced by the live M5 run (mass HTTP 503 rejection, ~168 accepted/s vs required >=1000/s) has no regression-guard once fixed; only a manual isolated-OS-user run catches it. arch-ctm flags this as blocking alongside the response-body-discard gap (AI33-M5-RESPONSE-BODY-DISCARDED)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-30T00:57:41Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-30T00:57:41Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI33-M5-NO-REAL-DAEMON-CI-TEST/AI33-M5-001> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-30T03:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:progressNote "AI33-M5-NINEFIX-QA-1: closed at a8d1e237. New test local_ipc_real_daemon_admission_burst_accepts_each_public_write (crates/atm-daemon/src/tests/runtime_root/local_ipc.rs:170-305) drives a real DaemonRequestDispatcher over serve_with_runtime_hooks on a genuine UDS/TCP-loopback socket via the public client transport, 16 concurrent threads, asserting each returns Sent -- not a mock. Wired into CI via `cargo test -p atm-daemon --verbose` on ubuntu/macos/windows matrix (.github/workflows/ci.yml:118,177). Independently confirmed by both req-qa and arch-qa. Non-blocking coverage-adequacy note from arch-qa: BURST_SIZE=16 is far below the 1000/s threshold that produced the original defect, so this test proves correctness of a small burst but does not itself regression-guard the specific capacity/backpressure failure mode -- flagged for awareness, not a reason to keep this finding open (test-coverage existence was the finding's scope)." ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

